#!/bin/sh
# Applies the data location chosen on the start page (form POST), through allod-data-api
# (which accepts only options its own scan offers, and erasing only when confirmed with
# the device name). Then back to the start page, which waits for the web UI.
# shellcheck source=../../../local/lib/allod/setup-html.sh disable=SC1091
. /usr/local/lib/allod/setup-html.sh

back() { # optional error message
  if [ -n "${1:-}" ]; then
    redirect "303 See Other" "/cgi-bin/start?error=$(printf '%s' "$1" | jq -sRr @uri)"
  else
    redirect "303 See Other" "/cgi-bin/start"
  fi
  exit 0
}

[ "${REQUEST_METHOD:-}" = POST ] || back
[ "${CONTENT_LENGTH:-0}" -le 4096 ] 2>/dev/null || back "bad request"
body=$(head -c "${CONTENT_LENGTH:-0}")
choice=$(form_value choice "$body")
confirm=$(form_value confirm "$body" | tr -d ' \t\r\n')
[ -n "$choice" ] || back "Choose a location first."
IFS='|' read -r kind dev start sectors <<EOF
$choice
EOF
# A short name (sdb1) confirms /dev/sdb1 as well.
case $confirm in /dev/*) ;; ?*) confirm="/dev/$confirm" ;; esac

reply=$(jq -cn --arg k "$kind" --arg d "$dev" --arg s "$start" --arg n "$sectors" --arg c "$confirm" \
  '{cmd: "apply", kind: $k, device: $d, start: $s, sectors: $n, confirm: $c}' | /usr/local/sbin/allod-data-api)
if printf '%s' "$reply" | jq -e '.ok' >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  back
fi
back "$(printf '%s' "$reply" | jq -r '.error // "failed"')"
